    [BugFix][MRV2] Skip non-Tensor KV cache components in block zeroer (#19598)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Skip non-Tensor components before calling `numel()` in the MRV2 KV block
    zeroer. This avoids initialization errors for nested tuple/list cache
    bindings while retaining the empty-Tensor guard from #18931.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Avoids the tuple/list `numel` exception while preserving zeroing of
    nonempty Tensor components. Nested containers remain excluded; this
    change does not unwrap them.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Python AST syntax check passed.
    
    A3-560T Nightly passed: `DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-W8A8-DSpark-PCP`
    ([run](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39925416578)).
    
    
